> Note: There are additional images in the source link. There is no US units conversion on the source site.

Preheat oven to 425°F.

If you have not bought @lamb{1.5%lb}(diced), cut your lamb shoulder or leg into large chunks and place to one side.

= Oil Marinade =
Mix @olive oil{1/3%cup} in a #small bowl{} with @garlic puree{1%tbsp},
@sundried tomato puree{1%tbsp}, @black pepper{}, and @salt{}.

Add @potatoes{1.25%lb}, @zucchini{1}(chopped chunky), @carrot{1%large}(chopped),
@green pepper{1}(chopped chunky), @eggplant{1%small}(chopped chunky), @onion{1%large}(chopped)
into a large #casserole dish{}.

Place lamb on top of the vegetables, pour the marinade and @white wine{1%cup} over the top.

Add @thyme{2%sprigs}, @rosemary{2%sprigs}, and @sage{2%sprigs}, trying to keep the herbs on top
so you can easily remove the herb stalks once cooked.
Use other herb mixes as desired.

Place lid on the casserole dish and cook for ~{90%minutes}.
If you do not have a lid, cover very well with kitchen foil.

Take the lid off, remove any thick herb stems.
Stir in @olive oil{2%tbsp}. Cook for a further ~{20-30%minutes}.

Serve with fresh homemade @bread to dip into the juices.

= Nutritional Info (per serving) =
632 kcal; fat 33g; saturated fat 6g; carbohydrates 41g; sugar 11g; protein 32g; fiber 8g; sodium 213mg
